lmn-gpo (7.3.4) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Build and release hardening only, no behaviour change: the catalog, the engine, the
    PowerShell scripts and the CLI are the same as in 7.3.3. Nothing has to be re-applied, no
    GPO is touched, `lmn-gpo apply` does not have to be run for this release.
  * The package is built from pinned inputs. The build container
    ghcr.io/linuxmuster/lmndev-runner:24.04 is pulled by its sha256 digest instead of a tag
    that upstream rebuilds every week, and every GitHub Action used by CI and the release is
    pinned to a commit instead of a movable tag. A new container or action version now
    arrives as a reviewable pull request (Renovate, never merged automatically) instead of
    silently changing what goes into the package.
  * The GitHub release no longer uses a third-party action. It is created as a draft, the
    .changes and every file it lists are uploaded and compared by sha256 with the build,
    and only then is the release published, so it can be made immutable: once published,
    its tag and files cannot be changed anymore. New among the files: the .buildinfo, which
    the .changes always named but the release did not carry.

