lmn-gpo (7.3.2) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * apply: FIX the loopback mode. LOOPBACK_MODE mapped merge to UserPolicyMode=2 and
    replace to 1 — Windows has it the other way round (GroupPolicy.admx, client event
    5311: 1 = Merge, 2 = Replace). Every pack in the catalog that carries loopback
    declares "merge", so with 7.3.1 and earlier all managed clients actually ran in
    REPLACE mode: GPOs linked only in the user's OU path (OU=Students, OU=Teachers, a
    class OU, GPOs from other tools) were dropped from the user's GPO list as soon as
    12-proxy-base or 15-lockdown-base was rolled out, without any error anywhere. In a
    stock linuxmuster domain this stayed invisible, because sophomorix' only user-effective
    GPO hangs at OU=<school> and is in the machine chain too. Measured and fixed against a
    real Windows 11 client (A/B with event 5311 and gpresult /scope user).
    ACTION: re-run `lmn-gpo apply --yes` once — the clients pick up UserPolicyMode=1 with
    the next `gpupdate /force` + reboot; event 5311 then says "Merge". No GPO has to be
    re-created.
  * doctor/apply: the loopback check reads the VALUE, not just the GPO name. After
    upgrading from 7.3.1 without a re-apply the existing 15-lockdown-base/12-proxy-base GPO
    still carries UserPolicyMode=2, so every client keeps running in Replace; doctor now
    says so ("its GPO still carries UserPolicyMode=2 (Replace), the catalog wants 1
    (Merge)") and names the fix instead of reporting the loopback as fine. apply prints the
    same for packs it is not going to rewrite in this run.
  * apply/doctor: new loopback prerequisite check. A pack with scope: school that carries
    USER settings (12-proxy-{student,teacher,staff}-schule) is linked to OU=Devices — a
    sibling of the user OUs — so it only ever reaches a user through loopback. Until now
    apply reported "Done: N GPO(s) applied." for GPOs that could not work. It now names
    the pack, the school and the packs that would fix it (12-proxy-base / 15-lockdown-base),
    per GPO and as a summary; doctor prints the same as a warning. Nothing is held back
    and no exit code changes — the GPOs themselves are correct.
  * scripts/lmn-gpo-check.ps1 expects UserPolicyMode=1 for "Loopback merge active".
  * README (EN + DE): the update section spells out that 7.3.2 needs one `lmn-gpo apply
    --yes` to take effect and that switching to Merge makes GPOs linked in the user OUs
    apply again on managed machines.
  * catalog: an unknown `loopback:` value is now an error at load time instead of silently
    switching loopback off.
  * README (EN + DE), docs/RESEARCH.md and the pack descriptions: the loopback values are
    Microsoft's (1 = Merge, 2 = Replace); the per-school user packs need a loopback pack;
    `remove` cannot take back the WinINET proxy values (ProxyEnable/ProxyServer/
    ProxyOverride) or the KMS host — they tattoo, with the commands to clear them; user
    policy is only processed in a real interactive session (a gpupdate /target:user over
    SSH/WinRM reports success and does nothing); `samba-tool gpo listall` without
    -U administrator hides the GPOs that deny Read to d_nopxe — use `lmn-gpo list --mine`.

