lmn-gpo (1.11.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Teacher Wi-Fi accepts SEVERAL networks. wlan_enterprise_networks is a list of
    {ssid, servernames, ca_cert}, each pinning its OWN RADIUS CA, so sites with separate
    RADIUS servers work; sites sharing one just reference the same file. Order is the
    connection preference.
    This is the roaming case: teachers travel between schools with their notebook, and
    because pack 13-wlan-enterprise is scope: global and filtered to @teachernb, one GPO at
    OU=SCHOOLS puts EVERY teacher SSID and EVERY CA on EVERY teacher notebook regardless of
    which school owns the device. Previously only a single teacher SSID could be configured,
    while the student PSK side had supported a list all along.
    The old single-key form (wlan_enterprise_ssid / _servernames / _ca_cert) is still
    honoured and folded into a one-element list, so existing site.yaml files keep working.
  * The generated script installs every CA into the machine trusted-root store before
    importing the profiles, and apply prints the pinned certificate per network
    ("MSG-LEHRER: RADIUS CA pinned: subject=... SHA1 ..."). A network whose CA file is
    missing is reported by name and skips the pack without retiring its GPO.
  * setup: the wizard now loops for teacher WLANs like it already did for student PSK
    networks, validates each CA on entry and shows its subject and thumbprint.

