lmn-gpo (1.10.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * New pack 10b-veyon-bandwidth-schule: cut the network load of Veyon classroom monitoring.
    Active automatically wherever Veyon is (requires: veyon), so no extra switch.
    Sets Master\ComputerMonitoringUpdateInterval to 2000 ms (Veyon default 1000),
    Master\ComputerMonitoringImageQuality to 3 = Low (default 2 = Medium) and
    Master\RemoteAccessImageQuality to 2 = Medium (default 0, which is genuinely LOSSLESS
    and makes a single remote-view session the biggest stream in the room). Roughly 3-5x
    less traffic in a busy classroom. All three are tunable in site.yaml via
    veyon_monitoring_interval_ms / veyon_monitoring_quality / veyon_remote_quality, with the
    enum clamped to 0-4 and the interval floored at 100 ms, because Veyon silently ignores an
    out-of-range value and falls back to its own default -- which would look like the pack
    doing nothing.
    Documented prominently, because it is the natural expectation and it is wrong: Veyon has
    NO "lower the resolution" setting. The Master receives every student's FULL framebuffer
    and only scales it down locally afterwards, and the thumbnail size is a per-user JSON
    value rather than a registry one, so smaller tiles save nothing on the wire. Frame rate
    and compression are the only real levers.
    Both keys are read by the Veyon MASTER, i.e. the teacher's PC, which therefore has to sit
    in the school's OU=Devices -- true when teachers use the ordinary classroom computers.
    Needs Veyon >= 4.8 on both sides; against an older client the master silently falls back
    to lossless.

