lmn-gpo (1.7.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * lmn-gpo-check.ps1: the time check now MEASURES instead of only reading configuration.
    w32tm /stripchart against the logon DC gives the real clock offset (language-neutral via
    /dataonly); under 2 s passes, beyond that it fails, and past 300 s it says plainly that
    Kerberos logons will break. MaxNegPhaseCorrection is checked as well, and both phase
    correction values are now asserted to be 0xFFFFFFFF -- if they are not, large offsets
    are silently never corrected, which is the dead-CMOS-battery case pack 17 exists for.
  * lmn-gpo-check.ps1: explain a MISSING Wi-Fi PSK profile instead of only reporting it.
    The script now reads the computer's own security groups from gpresult and walks the
    causes in order: membership in a d_*nopxe group (excluded BY DESIGN -- the machine is a
    teacher notebook and should carry the Enterprise profile), GPO filtered out, GPO never
    reached the machine, or the GPO applied but the startup script has not run yet, since
    machine startup scripts run at boot and a gpupdate is not enough. It also reports a
    stopped WLAN AutoConfig service, which silently prevents any profile import.
  * lmn-gpo-check.ps1: list the computer's device-group memberships under the applied GPOs,
    so it is visible which device filters can match at all.

